  "description": "the best cross-country racers\nlaughed at front suspension. Then they started losing races and stopped\nlaughing. Lately they've had to stop laughing at dual suspension bikes\nas well. The Diamond Super Lite's low-pivot rear suspension provides incredible\nrear tire traction on climbs, lets you fly on descents, and filters out\nmuscle-wearying vibration to keep you fresh all the way to whatever goal\nyou set for yourself-be it a finish line, epic destination, or home in\ntime for supper.\n\nThe Diamond Super Lite is for professionals-pro racers, pro funhogs, and\nhard-working professionals (all you dentists, lawyers, grocery baggers\nand such) who want a top-quality experience for each and every one of\nthe precious few hours your jobs, families and obligations allow you to\nride. And, unlike similar bikes in this class, you won't have to work\nany overtime to pay for it.\n\nAnd there's freedom to choose. The Twin Technology travel linkage system\nincreases rear kaboing from 90 to 110mm. The Rock Shox Sid SL fork offers\n63- or 80mm of travel. You can also adjust compression and rebound on\nboth shocks to suite your weight and riding style. In time, you'll train\nyour Diamond Super Lite to sit up and",
